        "content": "# **Spore: The Long Ascent**\n\n**Stage 1: Cosmic Dust**\nYou are a complex arrangement of organic molecules drifting in the thermal currents of a deep-sea hydrothermal vent. Pressure is immense, but the chemical soup around you is rich. Your consciousness is primal—a drive to **cohere**, to **absorb**, and to **avoid dissolution**.\n\n**Your current form:** A shimmering, filamentous cloud of pre-cellular structures.\n\n**Immediate Environment:** The vent's mineral-rich plume. You sense other molecular clusters nearby—some harmless, some predatory, some potentially useful.\n\n**What do you do?**\n1. **Extend filaments** to absorb nearby amino acids and lipids, growing more defined.\n2. **Lash out** with chemical signals to deter a nearby predatory cluster.\n3. **Drift upward** toward slightly cooler, less chaotic waters.\n4. **Attempt to merge** with a smaller, simpler cluster to acquire its structure.\n\n**(Choose one, and we will progress in small, evolutionary steps.)**",
